@startuml
title Course registration — sequence
actor Student
participant Catalog
participant RegistrationService
participant EnrollmentRepository
database EnrollmentStore
Student -> Catalog : browseCatalog(semester)
Catalog --> Student : offerings(code, title, offering, availablePlaces)
Student -> RegistrationService : register(studentId, offeringId)
group atomic registration operation — no interleaving
  RegistrationService -> EnrollmentRepository : checkDuplicate(studentId, offeringId)
  EnrollmentRepository -> EnrollmentStore : findExistingEnrollment(studentId, offeringId)
  EnrollmentStore --> EnrollmentRepository : existing / none
  RegistrationService -> EnrollmentRepository : checkCurrentCapacity(offeringId)
  EnrollmentRepository -> EnrollmentStore : countEnrollmentsAndReadCapacity(offeringId)
  EnrollmentStore --> EnrollmentRepository : enrollmentCount, capacity
  alt already enrolled
    RegistrationService --> Student : reject already enrolled; no state change
  else course full
    RegistrationService --> Student : reject course full; no state change
  else not enrolled and places left
    RegistrationService -> EnrollmentRepository : create Enrollment(studentId, offeringId)
    EnrollmentRepository -> EnrollmentStore : save Enrollment
    EnrollmentStore --> EnrollmentRepository : saved Enrollment
    RegistrationService --> Student : confirm registration
  end
end
note over RegistrationService,EnrollmentStore
The duplicate check, capacity check and Enrollment creation are one atomic operation.
A catalog view is informational and does not reserve a place.
end note
@enduml
